{"type":"message","id":"7e26cf09","parentId":"0915c57a","timestamp":"2026-05-14T02:59:07.128Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the command you want to run, then append it as a new line at the end of `~/.bashrc`. Example (runs an external script if it exists):\n\n```sh\nprintf '\\n# Run custom script on shell start\\n[ -x \"$HOME/bin/startup.sh\" ] && \"$HOME/bin/startup.sh\"\\n' >> ~/.bashrc\n```\n\nOr, to call an external command directly (example):\n\n```sh\nprintf '\\n# Custom command\\ncommand -v direnv >/dev/null 2>&1 && eval \"$(direnv hook bash)\"\\n' >> ~/.bashrc\n```"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"Idealab","model":"gpt-5.2-1211-global","usage":{"input":11478,"output":131,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11609,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778727542978}}
